      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When a patient's behavior seems erratic or unprovoked, focus heavily on grounding techniques and establishing basic safety. Avoid arguing against their perception or reacting to the perceived \"mischief,\" as this can escalate things quickly. Instead, redirect the focus to the immediate environment and their comfort, using simple, direct statements to anchor them in reality.",
      "source": "target",
