    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. Can you expand a bit on the communication side of things? Sometimes it feels like they aren't even listening to reason, almost like they're just behaving like little creatures or just trying to cause chaos for the sake of it. Is there a way to talk to someone when they're in that headspace without losing your own cool?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When reasoning isn't working, shift your focus from logical discourse to establishing connection and empathy. Use \"I\" statements—like, \"I'm here to help you feel better\"—rather than accusatory \"you\" statements. Maintain extreme patience and slow down your speech pace significantly, as a deliberate, calm rhythm can help regulate their own agitated system.",
